Store one declared contextStore secret using the exact input flags for its type. Stdin-backed replacement requires --yes.

Usage:
  bootwright secret set [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright secret set --name token --value-file ./token --yes

Flags:
      --certificate-file string   Read a certificate or CA bundle from a file
      --name string               Select the exact object name (required)
      --password-file string      Read a password from a file
      --password-stdin            Read a password from standard input
      --private-key-file string   Read a private key from a file
      --public-key-file string    Read an SSH public key from a file
      --username string           Store this username with a password
      --value-file string         Read a value from a file
      --value-stdin               Read a value from standard input
      --yes                       Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
